# One-line class and method docs

Every new or edited class, method, and function gets a single-line docstring that says what it does, not how.

- Put it on the class or `def`/`async def`, not on every statement.
- Skip only trivial one-line getters/setters that already say the same thing as the name.
- Do not write multi-paragraph docs unless the contract is non-obvious (errors, side effects, invariants).
- Apply the same habit in Python and in TypeScript (JSDoc one-liner on classes and exported functions).
